The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) calls every report in it one issue with one fix queued.
The reports describe three different bugs. Each one got its own ticket.

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October. The parser is fixed. The booking-v3 hint is won't fix,
because the booking-v3 form is retired. The engineering update says nothing about the one-day
move, so that ticket closed with no fix.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 was not one issue. If people still report a booking that moved by one day, reopen the
one-day ticket. The parser fix does not cover it.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

## What each one is

**`parser`.** The shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant in #4471 writes
the day first. 2 March comes out as 3 February. Fix it in the parser: read dates in the tenant's
order.

**`hint`.** The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People at day-first
tenants type what the hint says, month first, and the form reads it day first. Only form reports
from booking-v3 tenants land here. The parser fix does not touch this. The hint has to match the
tenant's order.

**`one-day`.** Some bookings move by one day and keep their month. A day and month swap cannot do
that. One meeting showed as Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday in Toronto, and one invite arrived
before its booking. That points at time zone conversion. The desk had already noted these
reports in `desk-notes.json`, but the #4471 table still counts them under `parser`.

## How the count works

- The export pages overlap, so some reports come twice. Count each id once.
- Place a report by its tenant: locale and booking form (`locales.ts`, `causes.ts`). Do not use
  the intake tag. Intake guesses it from the reporter's browser, so every en-US browser got
  `hint`, whatever the tenant runs.
- Read the body before you merge. A one-day move and a month flip share subject lines, so
  matching on subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put them together.

The table above runs on the export at build time. When the desk merges more reports into
#4471, the counts here follow.

